1. Data Cleaning

Removed units like kmpl, CC, bhp and kept only numeric values.

Filled missing numeric values with median (avoids influence of outliers).

Filled missing categorical values using mode (most common category).

2. Feature Engineering

Created Car_Age = 2024 - Year, giving a realistic age estimate.

Added Price_per_km to understand cost relative to usage.

3. Categorical Encoding

Converted Fuel_Type and Transmission into numerical dummy variables for better analysis.

4. dplyr-style Operations

Selected useful columns (Price, Mileage, Engine, Car_Age).

Filtered cars newer than 10 years.

Renamed Price → Used_Car_Price.

Sorted cars by price (high → low).

Computed average price by fuel type.

5. Key Insights

Higher mileage → lower price, which matches real-world depreciation.

Bigger engines and more power → higher prices.

Diesel cars show slightly higher average price compared to petrol.

Newer cars cost more, confirming normal market behavior.

6. Visual Findings

Price histogram shows most cars are in low–mid price range.

Mileage vs Price scatter shows decreasing trend.
